{"amendments":[{"body":"Make the new pre-step validation in `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs:490-492` non-mutating. `enforce_invariants` currently normalizes state in place at `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs:6-8`, `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs:95`, `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs:109-147`, and `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs:212-215` before it reaches the new hard failures at `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs:129` and `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs:185-210`. As a result, `step_hours(1)` can return `InvariantViolation` while still modifying the live engine; for example, a state with `water.ph = 9.0` and `shrimp_assimilation_efficiency = 1.2` comes back with `water.ph` clamped to `8.5`. Validate against a clone or split pure validation from normalization so rejected steps leave state untouched.","rationale":"This is a correctness/safety regression: failed preflight checks are no longer atomic and can silently discard existing state even though no simulation step ran."}],"summary":"I found one blocking issue in the new pre-step invariant enforcement: failed validation can still mutate engine state. The added invariant checks and save-load coverage otherwise look coherent."}